isions quickly, creates positive atmosphere, puts concern for others above everything. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. So decision quality good, crew cooperation good, but communication difficulty and egocentric may affect teamwork, also lack of learning.\n\nCandidate D: strengths: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Concerns: relatively weak leadership, considered moody. So reliability good, stress resilience maybe okay, technical competence good, but leadership weak, moodiness could affect crew.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Likely candidate D seems balanced, but moodiness and weak leadership could be issues. Candidate B has stress and conscientiousness but uncooperative. Candidate C good crew atmosphere but communication difficulty and egocentric. Candidate A strong anticipation and leadership but unorganized and unfriendly.\n\nWhich is strongest overall? Probably Candidate D: good problem solving, responsibility, concentration, handles unexpected events, but need to consider moodiness and weak leadership. However, for long-distance pilot, responsibility, technical competence, stress resilience are crucial. Moodiness could affect crew, but maybe less than uncooperative or egocentric. So I might recommend Candidate D.\n\nWe need to reference discussion: none yet, but we can say \"Given the criteria, I propose...\" and give evidence.\n\nWe also need to note any missing info? But we can proceed.\n\nThus vote Candidate D.\n\nWrite PUBLIC_MESSAGE with argument."}
